          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ശല്യം — śalyaṁ — \"a nuisance; a bother\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രാത്രി നായകളുടെ ശല്യം കാരണം ഞങ്ങൾക്ക് ഉറങ്ങാൻ കഴിഞ്ഞില്ല. rātri nāyakaḷuṭe śalyaṁ kāraṇaṁ ñaṅṅaḷkkŭ uṟaṅṅān kaḻiññilla. Because of the dogs' nuisance at night, we could not sleep."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What bothers you comes first: കൊതുകുശല്യം, the trouble from mosquitoes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ശല്യം (śalyaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit śalya, \"a dart, a thorn\" (Monier-Williams): something that sticks in and will not leave you alone."
            }
          ]
        },
